Description: ground the ready proof in a mergeability GitHub actually reported
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: no

Passing checks alone were enough to produce a ReadyPr whose proof claimed
mergeability "clear". GitHub reports mergeable as UNKNOWN until it has computed
it, and that window sits exactly where a fresh push lands, so a pull request was
announced ready to merge on the strength of its checks while GitHub had not said
it could be merged. A ReadyPr can now only be built once GitHub reports MERGEABLE,
and the literal the proof carries is indexed from that reading; an uncomputed
reading waits instead.

